E["subzone:sunnyglade"] = {t="subzone",n="Sunnyglade",z="riverglades",s="Twilight's Hammer zealots now occupy Sunnyglade's ruins in the Riverglades. Once a wealthy human settlement under Stormwind, it was devastated during the First War and abandoned as the Horde advanced.",h="Twilight's Hammer zealots now occupy Sunnyglade's ruins in the Riverglades.",sec={{t="Fall of a Golden Town",b="Before the First War, Sunnyglade was a wealthy human town. Then the Old Horde invasion shattered its peace. Orc raiders attacked and enslaved the residents who survived. Only a wizard's tower remained intact, for human conjurers to study the arcane arts.\n\nStormwind forces tried to free the captive peasants and rebuild Sunnyglade. But the Horde kept advancing through the Riverglades. Stormwind's commanders judged the outer province lost and drew resources back to defend the homeland. The town was left in ruins.",sp=0},{t="A Blighted Refuge",b="Sunnyglade lies far beyond the safe borders of Stormwind's restored realm. Its stone mage tower survived the First War and the years of abandonment. The peaceful township around it is gone, and Twilight's Hammer zealots now occupy the secluded ruins. They use the once-prosperous valley for their own designs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to Sunnyglade?",a="The Old Horde attacked and sacked Sunnyglade during the First War, enslaving its surviving residents. Human forces freed captive peasants and tried to rebuild, but Stormwind later abandoned the Riverglades to defend its homeland.",al={"what is sunnyglade","sunnyglade history","why is sunnyglade destroyed"}},{q="Who controls Sunnyglade now?",a="Twilight's Hammer cultists occupy Sunnyglade's ruins, including its broken houses and ancient wizard's tower.",al={"who lives in sunnyglade","sunnyglade enemies","sunnyglade twilight"}},{q="Why did the orcs leave the mage tower standing during the First War?",a="The Old Horde spared Sunnyglade's arcane tower so its warlocks and commanders could study human magic and seek to unravel its secrets.",al={"orc mage tower sunnyglade","sunnyglade tower lore"}},{q="Why didn't Stormwind reclaim the town after the war?",a="Stormwind's leaders judged the Riverglades lost as the First War intensified and redirected military resources to defend the homeland, leaving Sunnyglade behind.",al={"why abandoned","stormwind sunnyglade"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, Sunnyglade's lone wizard's tower recalls early human spellcraft. The Old Horde spared it so they could study human arcane knowledge.",["race:Human"]="As a human, Sunnyglade's overgrown stones recall the outer settlements Stormwind abandoned when it pulled back during the First War."},kw={"first war","mage tower","old horde","riverglades","stormwind","sunnyglade","twilight's hammer"},rel={"zone:riverglades","topic:twilight-s-hammer","topic:first-war","topic:old-horde","topic:stormwind-kingdom","zone:redridge"},src={"Sunnyglade"}}
E["zone:riverglades"] = {t="zone",n="Riverglades",z="riverglades",s="In Riverglades, human loyalists and Horde outposts still contest a valley east of the Badlands and Burning Steppes. Stormwind once claimed the region, but the Old Horde overran it in the First War. The Redridge Mountains lie southwest, the Swamp of Sorrows south, and Tanaris across the sea.",h="In Riverglades, human loyalists and Horde outposts still contest a valley east of the Badlands and Burning...",sec={{t="A Forgotten Borderland",b="Before the First War, Riverglades belonged to the Kingdom of Stormwind. Then the Old Horde swept through. Orcs sacked Sunnyglade but spared its mage tower to study human sorcery. They enslaved the townsfolk who survived. Stormwind soldiers tried to free the captives and rebuild, but the kingdom judged the valley lost and sent its strength to defend the core homelands. For years, the crown gave Riverglades little formal support.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Farholde",b="Stormwind's leaders left Riverglades behind, yet its human defenders never fully surrendered their homeland. Knight Commander Demar Brant leads the remaining loyalists of the legendary brotherhood of the horse. They hold farholde keep against the wilderness and hostile invaders. Nearby, the modern Horde keeps a strong presence at outposts such as rog'mar and bolder'ok. The old struggle over the glades continues.",sp=0},{t="Geography and Travel",b="Riverglades follows the coast of the Forbidding Sea, among mountains and winding waterways. You can cross west through Blackrock Pass to the Burning Steppes, or travel southwest through Redridge Pass to the Redridge Mountains. South lies the Swamp of Sorrows. To the northwest, trails pass Twilight's Shroud into the Badlands. At powderfuse port, you can take a boat across the sea to steamwheedle port in Tanaris.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Riverglades?",a="Riverglades lies east of the Badlands and Burning Steppes, along the Forbidding Sea. Stormwind once claimed the region. Now the Alliance holds Farholde Keep while the Horde keeps Rog'mar.",al={"riverglades overview","what is this zone","about riverglades"}},{q="What happened to Sunnyglade?",a="The Old Horde raided and destroyed Sunnyglade during the First War. Orcs enslaved the surviving villagers but kept a local mage tower intact to study human magic. Stormwind soldiers tried to free the captives and rebuild, but the kingdom finally abandoned the area to defend its western borders.",al={"sunnyglade history","fall of sunnyglade","what happened to the town"}},{q="Who controls Farholde Keep?",a="Alliance loyalists hold Farholde Keep under Knight Commander Demar Brant of the Brotherhood of the Horse. His forces have spent years fighting to reclaim Riverglades after Stormwind gave the territory up as lost.",al={"who leads farholde","alliance in riverglades","Brotherhood of the Horse"}},{q="How do you reach Tanaris from the Riverglades?",a="From Powderfuse Port on Riverglades' eastern shore, a coastal boat runs regularly to Steamwheedle Port in Tanaris, crossing directly over the sea.",al={"boat to tanaris","Powderfuse Port boat","how to get to tanaris"}},{q="What passes lead into other zones?",a="You can travel southwest through Redridge Pass to reach the Redridge Mountains, or head south toward the Swamp of Sorrows. Westward, Blackrock Pass leads past the Bristle Hills to the Burning Steppes. Trails north of Twilight's Shroud run directly into the Badlands.",al={"how to get to redridge","passes from riverglades","exits from riverglades"}},{q="What is Krol'dok Stronghold?",a="Krol'dok Stronghold is a fortified dungeon complex in Riverglades and a major seat of hostile power in the contested territory.",al={"kroldok stronghold","riverglades dungeon","what dungeon is here"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance soldier, you find old wounds laid bare in Riverglades. Remnants of the Brotherhood of the Horse continue their quiet crusade to retake land Stormwind abandoned during the First War.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, outposts such as Rog'mar secure a coastal foothold and keep pressure on the old human strongholds east of Redridge.",["race:Human"]="As a human, you can see a tragic chapter of your heritage in Sunnyglade. It recalls the heavy toll the First War took on your kingdom's eastern frontier."},kw={"blackrock pass","Brotherhood of the Horse","demar brant","Farholde Keep","krol'dok stronghold","Powderfuse Port","redridge pass","riverglades","Rog'mar","sunnyglade"},rel={"subzone:sunnyglade","subzone:blackrock-pass","zone:redridge","zone:badlands","zone:swampofsorrows","zone:burningsteppes","subzone:steamwheedle-port"},src={"Riverglades"}}
